Z||000000||GT Bastard||09-10-2000||04:27 AM||||These pics were taken in Sioux Falls, SD at Brad Hatle's(friend of mine) shop.  He doesn't stictly do Fiero work, but he's into other stuff as well. It just so happens that there is a mass quantity of Fiero's in Sioux Falls and he's worked on just about every one. I found him one day while cruising around a local neighborhood and saw several Fiero's parked outside.  The Fiero in the pictures belongs to the kid with the grimey hand(Brads cousin.)  It's his very first car, and Brad helped him put it together for under 600 bucks.  It's an '86SE with a blown motor that is now a good running car.   Brads done just about everything you can do to a Fiero several times over, so contact me if you're in need of an experienced mechanic(mrbios@LL.net) <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BRAD1.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BRAD2.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BRAD3.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BRAD4.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BRAD5.JPG"> <P>PS--  Brad wanted me to mention.... Don't give him any crap about pulling the motor from the top!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>   ||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||09-10-2000||04:30 AM||||ps... sorry the quality of these pictures is rather crappy.  My scanner is no picnic either.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Chris Schaefer||09-10-2000||09:06 AM||||If pulling the motor through the top is his preferred way then so be it.  I personal do not like the idea.  All I can think of is one wrong move and then.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Crap, there goes the rear window.  I would not want to have to install a new one.  Also it just seems like so much more work.<P>Anyhow, it is good to know that there will be another Fiero back on the road. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW, the pictures came through just fine. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||4
